  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116458",
      "title": "Adding Static Data To Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 290,
      "videoOrder": 277,
      "sourceHash": "11bdcc072ef9142c3c6a1f9c6f457c4419e66c98b2b5137d011f3c5940eb8875",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 2.88,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmuller] So now at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.88,
          "end": 6.81,
          "en": "you did learn a lot about routing in Angular apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.81,
          "end": 11.81,
          "en": "but there is even more the Angular router offers to us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.03,
          "end": 16.62,
          "en": "For example, you can also leverage the Angular router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.62,
          "end": 20.55,
          "en": "to fetch and prepare data for your routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.55,
          "end": 23.43,
          "en": "so for your Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.43,
          "end": 26.49,
          "en": "For example here, for this route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.49,
          "end": 28.83,
          "en": "this users/:userId route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.83,
          "end": 30.933,
          "en": "that loads the UserTasksComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.58,
          "end": 35.58,
          "en": "This component uses some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.58,
          "end": 39.33,
          "en": "or needs to fetch some data internally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.33,
          "end": 43.47,
          "en": "It needs to, in the end, fetch the username of the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.47,
          "end": 46.02,
          "en": "for whom the tasks should be displayed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.02,
          "end": 49.32,
          "en": "And that username depends on the route parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.32,
          "end": 52.83,
          "en": "because it, in the end, depends on that userId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.83,
          "end": 54.393,
          "en": "that's part of the path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.16,
          "end": 60.24,
          "en": "Now, currently, I'm fetching that username here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.24,
          "end": 63.63,
          "en": "in ngOnInit by subscribing to changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.63,
          "end": 65.37,
          "en": "to my route parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.37,
          "end": 69.99,
          "en": "and by then getting the username from the usersService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.99,
          "end": 72.53999999999999,
          "en": "Alternatively, as you saw before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.53999999999999,
          "end": 74.7,
          "en": "we could've worked with Signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.7,
          "end": 77.733,
          "en": "and for example, use a computed Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.57,
          "end": 82.92,
          "en": "but there's yet another option you could use to fetch data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.92,
          "end": 84.36,
          "en": "for a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.36,
          "end": 86.55,
          "en": "an option that would allow you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.55,
          "end": 89.91,
          "en": "to keep your component class leaner,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.91,
          "end": 92.31,
          "en": "which is something you might wanna do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.31,
          "end": 94.53,
          "en": "So an option that in the end allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.53,
          "end": 99.18,
          "en": "to get this data fetching code here out of this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.18,
          "end": 102.3,
          "en": "which you don't have to do, but which you might wanna do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.3,
          "end": 105.18,
          "en": "because there definitely also is some merit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.18,
          "end": 108.84,
          "en": "to having lean, clean Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.84,
          "end": 112.68,
          "en": "Because Angular's router actually allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.68,
          "end": 116.13,
          "en": "to define a data property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.13,
          "end": 120.54,
          "en": "on your routes, so in your route configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.54,
          "end": 123.54,
          "en": "There are indeed many properties you can add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.54,
          "end": 128.1,
          "en": "and we'll explore other important ones like canMatch later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.1,
          "end": 129.78,
          "en": "but there for example also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.78,
          "end": 132.9,
          "en": "is this data property I just mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.9,
          "end": 137.19,
          "en": "And this data property in the end allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.19,
          "end": 140.4,
          "en": "to define some data object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.4,
          "end": 144.66,
          "en": "And that data object can hold any key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.66,
          "end": 145.683,
          "en": "of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.73,
          "end": 149.76,
          "en": "Like for example, message: 'Hello!'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.76,
          "end": 153.12,
          "en": "which is not too meaningful here for this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.12,
          "end": 155.43,
          "en": "but which allows me to introduce you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.43,
          "end": 158.52,
          "en": "to this data object and how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.52,
          "end": 163.11,
          "en": "So you can set any arbitrary static data of your choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.11,
          "end": 165.87,
          "en": "for a route and the routed component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.87,
          "end": 170.28,
          "en": "with help of that data property on the route configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.28,
          "end": 173.22,
          "en": "And if you do so, you can go to the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.22,
          "end": 175.26,
          "en": "that is loaded by this route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.26,
          "end": 178.673,
          "en": "so in this case the UserTasksComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.673,
          "end": 179.506,
          "en": "And in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.506,
          "end": 184.506,
          "en": "you can get hold of that data in two main ways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.53,
          "end": 188.73,
          "en": "If you enabled this ComponentInputBinding here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.73,
          "end": 191.01,
          "en": "in the route configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.01,
          "end": 196.01,
          "en": "any data key that is set up here, like message in my case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.53,
          "end": 200.19,
          "en": "will be provided as an input to the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.19,
          "end": 201.663,
          "en": "that's loaded for the route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.5,
          "end": 203.64,
          "en": "So in my case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.64,
          "end": 208.38,
          "en": "this UserTasksComponent will receive a message property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 208.38,
          "end": 212.19,
          "en": "a message input, because I added this data here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 212.19,
          "end": 215.94299999999998,
          "en": "and because I have withComponentInputBinding enabled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.93,
          "end": 220.68,
          "en": "Therefore in this component, we could accept that input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.68,
          "end": 224.82,
          "en": "We would get our message here as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.82,
          "end": 227.073,
          "en": "for example, with that input function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 228.21,
          "end": 231.9,
          "en": "And I know that I'll get a string here in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.9,
          "end": 235.95,
          "en": "and I can even make this required here since I know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 235.95,
          "end": 238.32,
          "en": "that this will be set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.32,
          "end": 241.353,
          "en": "because I'm setting that message data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 243.54,
          "end": 245.82,
          "en": "Well, and then, we could use that, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 245.82,
          "end": 248.22,
          "en": "here to keep things simple,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 248.22,
          "end": 252.33,
          "en": "I can console.log, Input Data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 252.33,
          "end": 254.76,
          "en": "and then simply output this.message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 254.76,
          "end": 258.153,
          "en": "and read that input here in ngOnInit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 259.53,
          "end": 263.34,
          "en": "With that, in this application, if I select a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 263.34,
          "end": 266.1,
          "en": "I see that input data being locked here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 266.1,
          "end": 267.963,
          "en": "and that's my message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 269.94,
          "end": 273.96,
          "en": "So that's how you could pass some static data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 273.96,
          "end": 277.56,
          "en": "like this static string to a route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 277.56,
          "end": 280.05,
          "en": "but that's not ultimately what I wanna do here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 280.05,
          "end": 280.95,
          "en": "because here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 280.95,
          "end": 284.55,
          "en": "I mentioned that I wanna outsource this data fetching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 284.55,
          "end": 288.18,
          "en": "and that's of course not static data but dynamic data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 288.18,
          "end": 292.56,
          "en": "because it depends on the userId route parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 292.56,
          "end": 294.27,
          "en": "So that's therefore what we'll do next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 294.27,
          "end": 295.86,
          "en": "But it's also worth knowing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 295.86,
          "end": 299.01,
          "en": "that if you had some static data, you could provide it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 299.01,
          "end": 300.93,
          "en": "with that data property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 300.93,
          "end": 303.27,
          "en": "But now, we're going to take that data fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 303.27,
          "end": 304.323,
          "en": "to the next level.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
